      "content": "The Right to Repair is crucial because it fundamentally challenges the \"right to fix\" that big tech often claims for its specialized, proprietary systems. By making parts and diagnostic information available, the movement directly fights planned obsolescence, which is the deliberate design of products to break down and force new sales. This fight is essential for economic fairness, as it democratizes the right to own and maintain the property you purchase, breaking the cycle of mandatory, high-cost corporate support.",
